        }
      ],
      "why": "pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, so throughput_msps = Fmax. To meet throughput_msps >= 32, Fmax must be >= 32 MHz, which is easily met. The sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5us constraint requires that 32 back-to-back requests complete within 0.5us. With 1 result/cycle and Fmax >= 32MHz, 32 cycles take <= 1us at 32MHz, but we need <= 0.5us, so Fmax must be >= 64 MHz. A fully pipelined CORDIC with N stages has N+2 latency; for N=14-18, latency is 16-20 cycles. At 64MHz, 20 cycles = 312ns < 500ns, so the batch constraint is met. The accuracy constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-12 = 0.000244 requires accuracy_bits >= 12. For CORDIC, accuracy is roughly 2^-(N+1) for the rotation, so N >= 13 gives ~2^-14 accuracy. data_width 16-20 with n_iter 14-18 should comfortably meet 12-bit accuracy. Minimising area means we want the smallest data_width and n_iter that still meet accuracy, so the search should focus on the lower end of these ranges. angle_guard and frac_guard affect accuracy margin; small values (0-2) should suffice for 12-bit accuracy with N>=14."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
